# 7. Layer Responsibilities

## 7.1 Presentation Layer

Owns:

- SwiftUI screens
- View composition
- View-specific state
- Accessibility presentation
- Navigation bindings
- Motion and haptic requests
- User-facing copy

Does not own:

- Networking
- Persistence
- Vendor APIs
- Scene execution logic
- Automation evaluation
- Device identity
- Retry policy

## 7.2 Application Layer

Owns use cases and orchestration.

Examples:

- Load dashboard
- Run scene
- Add device
- Change device state
- Create automation
- Run diagnostics
- Restore navigation

Application services translate user intent into domain operations.

## 7.3 Domain Layer

Owns:

- Core entities
- Value objects
- Capability model
- Command model
- Scene definitions
- Automation definitions
- Errors
- Policies
- Repository protocols

The Domain layer must remain platform-independent Swift where practical.

## 7.4 Infrastructure Layer

Owns technical implementations of domain contracts.

Examples:

- File persistence
- Keychain
- Network clients
- Clock
- Logger
- App lifecycle adapter
- Notification scheduling

## 7.5 Integration Layer

Owns vendor and framework adapters.

Each integration contains:

- Discovery provider
- Pairing coordinator
- API or framework adapter
- Resource mapper
- Capability resolver
- Command executor
- Event synchronizer
- Diagnostics provider

