# 9. Module Boundaries

Initial code may live in one Xcode application target while preserving logical module boundaries.

As the project grows, recommended Swift packages are:

```text
AuraDomain
AuraApplication
AuraDesignSystem
AuraDiagnostics
AuraSceneEngine
AuraAutomationEngine
AuraDeviceDiscovery
AuraIntegrations
AuraTestSupport
```

Vendor integrations may later become separate packages when their dependencies and build times justify it.

Do not split into packages merely for appearance.

A package boundary is justified when it improves:

- Compilation isolation
- Test isolation
- Ownership
- Reuse
- Dependency control

