# 61. Failure Scenarios

## Scenario A: One plugin fails at startup

Expected:

- App opens normally
- Other integrations continue
- Failed plugin reports degraded health
- User receives contextual recovery

## Scenario B: Persistence is unavailable

Expected:

- App avoids destructive overwrite
- Critical error is diagnosed
- In-memory fallback may permit limited use
- Recovery guidance is shown

## Scenario C: Network changes during a command

Expected:

- Outcome becomes confirmed, failed or unknown
- Unsafe duplicate retry is avoided
- Targeted rediscovery begins where appropriate

## Scenario D: Scene partially fails

Expected:

- Successful actions remain recorded
- Failed actions are identified
- Scene result is partial success
- Retry may target failed safe actions only

## Scenario E: UI disappears during async work

Expected:

- View-owned tasks cancel
- Engine-owned operations continue only when appropriate
- No released view model receives updates

