# 62. Acceptance Criteria

The App Architecture is accepted when:

1. The codebase has explicit Presentation, Application, Domain, Infrastructure and Integration boundaries.
2. SwiftUI does not call vendor APIs directly.
3. Domain models do not import vendor frameworks.
4. The Unified Device Registry is the source of truth for logical devices.
5. Device identity remains stable across network address changes.
6. Integrations conform to shared, minimal contracts.
7. Scene and Automation Engines operate independently of SwiftUI.
8. Mutable shared state is actor-isolated.
9. Every external boundary is mockable.
10. Credentials are stored only through the approved credential service.
11. Diagnostics are available across all major subsystems.
12. Errors are translated before presentation.
13. Optimistic state never masquerades as confirmed security state.
14. Navigation uses typed routes.
15. Cached state allows fast startup without pretending stale state is live.
16. Plugin failures remain isolated.
17. App lifecycle and cancellation are handled explicitly.
18. Core user journeys are covered by automated tests.
19. Real hardware is used for integration validation.
20. The architecture supports future clients without requiring vendor logic inside UI layers.

